      "summary": "The new lock closes the race when a replacement changes the basis ID or version. Because SetCurrentBasis permits different basis contents with the same ID and version, the captured basis can still be superseded before the locked submission check.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Investigation/AssessmentStore.cs",
          "line": 32,
          "message": "RunIfCurrent treats a replacement with the same basis ID and version as the captured basis, so a same-version update can still allow submission from stale evidence.",
          "confidence": 0.84,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Assess captures the current basis and validates claims against its documents. RunIfCurrent then considers the captured basis current when only BasisId and BasisVersion match; SetCurrentBasis accepts a replacement without enforcing a version change.",
            "failureScenario": "Assess captures basis version 3 and validates a claim against its documents. Before RunIfCurrent, another call stores different documents or coverage under the same basis ID and version. The check passes and inbox.Submit creates a request using the captured, superseded basis. This leaves the prior stale-basis finding reachable for same-version replacements (OWASP A08:2025)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
